# Files that live in this directory but must not be served from it.
# Same syntax as .gitignore; wrangler skips anything matched here when
# uploading static assets. Without this, flarepeek.com/wrangler.jsonc and
# /README.md would both be publicly fetchable.
wrangler.jsonc
README.md

# `wrangler dev --config site/wrangler.jsonc` writes its local miniflare state
# here, inside the asset directory. Without this line those .sqlite files get
# uploaded and served — previewing the site would silently publish scratch
# state to flarepeek.com.
.wrangler
